What transformation maps shape $A$ to shape $B$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0)--(1.5,0)--(1.5,0.7)--(0.6,0.7)--(0.6,1.7)--(0,1.7)--cycle;
\draw (3.2,0.8)--(4.7,0.8)--(4.7,1.5)--(3.8,1.5)--(3.8,2.5)--(3.2,2.5)--cycle;
\node[below] at (0.75,0) {$A$};
\node[below] at (3.95,0.8) {$B$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

What transformation maps the shaded arrow to the unshaded arrow?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[fill=gray!25] (-2.5,0.3)--(-1.2,0.3)--(-1.2,-0.3)--(-0.3,0.7)--(-1.2,1.7)--(-1.2,1.1)--(-2.5,1.1)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (0,-0.7)--(0,2.1);
\draw (2.5,0.3)--(1.2,0.3)--(1.2,-0.3)--(0.3,0.7)--(1.2,1.7)--(1.2,1.1)--(2.5,1.1)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

What transformation maps arrow $P$ to arrow $Q$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (C) at (0,0);
\draw[->] (0.6,0.6)--(2.4,0.6);
\draw[->] (-0.6,0.6)--(-0.6,2.4);
\fill (C) circle (1.5pt);
\node[below] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above] at (1.5,0.6) {$P$};
\node[right] at (-0.6,1.5) {$Q$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which description maps segment $MN$ to segment $M'N'$?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[gray!30,very thin] (0,0) grid (7,4);
\draw (0.5,3.4)--(2.5,3.4);
\draw (4.5,0.4)--(6.5,0.4);
\node[above] at (0.5,3.4) {$M$};
\node[above] at (2.5,3.4) {$N$};
\node[below] at (4.5,0.4) {$M'$};
\node[below] at (6.5,0.4) {$N'$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
